    "risk_summary": "A fine F is 3.820 meV/atom higher than B, its residual full-stress maximum is 0.488 GPa, and Re–Tc decomposition remains a competing prior. ReTc3 in the literature is Tc-rich and must not be aliased with this Re3Tc state.",
    "ambient_scope": "Exact model force/full stress, converged electronic outputs, reported finite-q workflow and raw Γ optical evidence provide a bounded near-ambient source-model screen. Source residual stress/metastable alternatives remain explicit; this is not proof of synthesizeability, full BZ or global equilibrium.",
    "route_response": "Ordered tetragonal Re-rich A versus L12 B has all-ten λ gain and all separate fixed-μ Tc products favor A (Eliashberg +0.710 K). The like-Tc network differs by about 1.135 Å. Complete species-channel geometry differences and computed all-σ pairing response are saved against the frozen controls. Cell/grid/method sensitivity prevents a pure geometry-only causal claim; no bandwidth/carrier quantity is substituted.",
